  "translate_en|mods/Makeshift Crossbow/42.14/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox_EN.txt|Sandbox_MSXBow_Retrieval_tooltip": "Determines the likelihood of being able to recover fired bolts. <br> With default settings, recovery chance scales with maintenance level.",
  "translate_en|mods/Makeshift Crossbow/42.14/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip_EN.txt|Tooltip_MSXBow.BoltFlights": "Thin, feathered membrane intended to stabilize the trajectory of a bolt.",
  "translate_en|mods/Makeshift Crossbow/42.14/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip_EN.txt|Tooltip_MSXBow.BoltShaft": "Narrow, carved wooden shafts suitable as the trunk of a projectile. Needs a few more parts before it can be fired.",
  "translate_en|mods/Makeshift Crossbow/42.14/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip_EN.txt|Tooltip_MSXBow.CrossbowBolt": "A flimsy, makeshift projectile more suited for target practice than actual defense. Still, it will do in a pinch.",
  "translate_en|mods/Makeshift Crossbow/42.14/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip_EN.txt|Tooltip_MSXBow.Makeshift_Crossbow": "A ramshackle construction of various odds and ends. Fires quiet, short-range bolts for rather unimpressive damage. Better than nothing.",
  "translate_en|mods/Makeshift Crossbow/42.14/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip_EN.txt|Tooltip_MSXBow.PrepperMag": "A limited-run periodical marketed as a survival guide for the 'End of Days'; the intended addressee probably won't miss it.<br>Provides direction in constructing a makeshift crossbow and ammo from everyday items.",
  "translate_en|mods/Makeshift Crossbow/42.14/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip_EN.txt|Tooltip_Recipe_MaintainStock": "Being a rough, wooden implement, the stock of the bow needs to be inspected and maintained to prevent stress-related failure.",
  "translate_en|mods/Makeshift Crossbow/42.14/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip_EN.txt|Tooltip_Recipe_RestringBow": "Over countless uses, the elasticicty of the crossbow string degrades and the system loses efficacy. Proactively replacing the string <br> can attempt to remedy this. Much less material-intensive than a rebuild.",
